>I'm sure someone has answered this, but....
>
>how should I go about uncursing HUGE quantities of items (found a ghost
>level, killed off all the ghosts, and now have a pile of cursed stuff that
>would be fine if it wasn't cursed)?  I know that a blessed remove curse
>scroll will remove the curse from all items in your pack, but what about
>stuff you aren't carrying?

Spoilers ahead (sort of)


There is no wand of remove curse, so you can't uncurse a pile of stuff.

Get a pile of scrolls that you don't care for (punishment, destroy armor,
light, detect monsters, etc.).  Dip them in a fountain.  Use your magic marker
to write remove curse on them all.  Drop them on an altar and group them all
together.  Dip them in a potion of holy water (one potion will get them all).
Then drop all the good stuff in your pack except your weapon and maybe the
rings you're wearing.  Do an assembly-line remove curse on the batch of stuff,
using one scroll each time you have picked up all the items you can carry.

Of course I usually don't waste scrolls on uncursing that much stuff, when
much of it will turn out to be useless anyway.  I just try to pick out the
good stuff.



